Globe-nominated actress

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from the "Divergent
films franchise

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the hit series
"Big Little Lies."

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
She stars in "The Last Lette
from Your Lover,"

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:12.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is streaming on Netfli
on July 23rd.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.481 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:17.550 line:92%
-Come. Mr. Booth, dance with me.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.852 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Have fun, my friend.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-♪♪ Is slowly
going on the rocks now ♪♪

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.558 line:92%
♪♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:29.162 line:92%
♪♪ Tell me, tell me, baby

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:34.901
♪♪ Whatcha gonna do 'bout it
Whatcha gonna do 'bout it? ♪

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.903 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪ Oh, tell me ♪♪

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:39.439
-Please welcome back to the show
Shailene Woodley.

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.641 line:92%
Hello, Shailene. How are you

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.644 line:92%
-Hi. I'm so good. How are you?

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:45.245 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm wonderful.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:47.047
I mean, we've talked in the past
about the fact

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:50.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you are not particularl
good with new technology,

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:54.521
and seeing you there in a film
that takes place in the '60s

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:58.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
that must have been one of
the many draws to the project.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:02.429
-Yeah. The fact that there was
no cellphones and no laptops

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.630 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
was a major bonus.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's so funny just watchin
that clip right now,

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:09.135
seeing, like, those dance move
and the music. It really just --

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's something
that was so transformative

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
about pretending
to live in that space

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that era where you actuall
had human connection.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had two people
touching one another

00:01:18.678 --> 00:01:22.582
instead of everything bein
through this 2-D screen.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.383 line:92%
-And it's interesting, you know,

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's also obviously
about letter writing.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:28.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you are someone who
even in this modern day and ag

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
will write a letter.
Is this true?

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I love letters.
I love me some letters!

00:01:33.026 --> 00:01:35.628
There's nothing better
than opening your mailbox

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.362 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and putting a letter in

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:39.966
and having the anticipation of
"When's it going to get there?

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:40.800 line:92%
What are they going to think

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are they going
to like what I wrote?"

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.736 line:92%
And then also receiving them

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just --
I'm a hopeless romantic,

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:48.842
and there's something that's
just very, very romantic to me

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:49.642 size:78% position:39% line:92%
about letter writing.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think I have two friend
who to this day

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
will still write
a handwritten thank-you letter

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like
the only two friends

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:01.054
that I want to be at my funeral,
'cause they're the only ones

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:03.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were nice enough
to take the time.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
I think that's what it is.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
When somebody writes me
even an e-mail --

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know that's not
a handwritten letter,

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:12.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
but when someone takes the tim
to write something out,

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:13.766 size:88% position:44% line:92%
write their feelings out

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
and express what they're
experiencing in life,

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:20.440
it just hits a different part of
my core than, "Hey, how are you?

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ha, ha. Did you see
that game last night?"

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think as long
as they spell it Y-O-U

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
instead of just
a solitary "U" --

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:29.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't. I cannot.
Thank goodness --

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:31.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember
when texting first started

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.052 line:92%
and it was like "TTYL," "BRB"?

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:36.789 size:84% position:42%
"LOL" is still a thing,
but those ones -- Whew!

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, the heartbreaking
thing now is

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:40.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
there are just new ones
that I would have no idea.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:42.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the saddest thing
is when I google,

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:46.199 line:92%
"What do these letters mean?

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.267 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's so true.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, obviously this is -
This show is about --

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
This film, I should say, i
about romance. Did you have --

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:57.010
Were there romantic films that
you were drawn to growing up

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.611 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Do you have favorites?

00:02:58.611 --> 00:02:59.579 line:92%
-So many. I didn't really --

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:01.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
We didn't watch a lot of T
when I was growing up.

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
But my mom, whenever
she'd be folding laundry

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
or doing the dishes
or some sort of benign task,

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
she always had "Pretty Woman
or "Dirty Dancing"

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:12.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
or "Romancing the Stone"
or "Notting Hill" on.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:15.562
And so those were kind of
the movies that I was raised on.

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:18.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was my filmography
when I was a child.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:19.866 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, I just watched --

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
My wife made me watch "Notting
Hill" for the first time.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had somehow missed it,
and just an A-plus.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
It really holds up
incredibly well.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's so good, right?
-Yeah.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:28.808 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Oh, it's just so --

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:32.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
It never gets old.
The music, it's so --

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:32.879 size:84% position:42% line:92%
The cast. It's perfect.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:36.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also -- Speaking
of romance, you managed to do,

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:38.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
on a year where so many
relationships ended

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:42.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
during a pandemic,
you managed to start one.

00:03:42.355 --> 00:03:44.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations
on your engagement.

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:45.625 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you so much.

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:47.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you. Yeah, I always laug
with my friends.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:50.663 size:84% position:42%
I'm like, "Y'all either
got divorced, engaged,

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:51.531 size:88% position:44% line:92%
married, or had a baby."

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:55.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, that summed up everyone'
quarantine experience.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.336 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:59.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- Now, I've been
fortunate enough

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
to meet Aaron Rodgers
a few times.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:05.245
And I, of course, have read that
you are not a giant sports fan

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:06.679 line:92%
I know that he is not someon

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
who is only
interested in sports.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:12.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has a giant
breadth of interests.

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:12.852 line:92%
But have you felt the need

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:17.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
to sort of bone up a little bi
on your sports terminology

00:04:17.657 --> 00:04:20.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, I guess I haven't fel
any pressure to,

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:22.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's exciting, you know,
to get behind --

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:25.031
The Packers games are the only
ones I find really interesting

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.966 size:78% position:39%
'cause I have people
to actually root for.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:32.305
But it is a whole new world,
learning all of the different --

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:35.008 size:88% position:44%
I still am always like,
"Oh, you scored a goal!"

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.409 line:92%
He's like, "It's a touchdown."

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:38.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or I'll be like,
"You crossed the line,"

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's like, "It's a yard,
or whatever.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
I still can't --
I still can't get it right

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm learning,
slowly but surely.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just like that there's
something passive-aggressive

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
about saying,
"You crossed the line."

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:50.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he'd be like,
"Is this about the game

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:52.925 line:92%
or something I did last night?

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.227 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.195 size:75% position:38% line:92%
He sort of -- His --

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:59.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
Great outside of, obviously,
an incredible season,

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:02.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
his pandemic accomplishmen
was hosting "Jeopardy!"

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:05.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
Assuming he took it a seriousl
as he takes game prep,

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:08.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
how much "Jeopardy!"
did you have to watch with him

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:11.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Luckily -- I mean,
I was filming in Montreal

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:14.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he was prepping
for "Jeopardy!" And so I -

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:15.715 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And he was quarantining.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I would go to work
at 8:00 a.m., 6:00 a.m.,

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he would start his Netflix
"Jeopardy!" binge.

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:24.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then when I would get home
at 8:00 or 9:00 p.m.,

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:26.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
he would still be
watching "Jeopardy!"

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.660 line:92%
And I would open the trash can

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would just see like
bunch of empty to-go container

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
and milkshake cups that he had
ordered on Uber Eats.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"You literally just Uber Eated

00:05:35.001 --> 00:05:37.070 size:84% position:42%
and watched 'Jeopardy!'
all day long today."

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like,
"Yeah, look at my notes."

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:41.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he had stacks of notebooks
of notes that he took

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:43.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
and highlighted
and went back through.

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:44.744 line:92%
It was actually really inspiring

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:46.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
to watch his steadfast
commitment

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:50.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
to learning every single par
of the "Jeopardy!" game.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:52.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we did a lot of rehearsing
back and forth

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:56.589
where he would read some fak
things that he had created

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.458 line:92%
and be like, "Was my tone right?

00:05:58.458 --> 00:06:00.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was the connotation
of this right?

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.861 size:84% position:42% line:92%
How is it all working?"

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.162 size:88% position:44% line:92%
[ Chuckles ] It was fun.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.731 line:92%
-Well, the preparation paid off.

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:07.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to ask you
about a story I read recently.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:09.168 size:75% position:38%
You know, obviously,
one of the fun parts

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:12.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
about being in show business
is you meet new co-stars,

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:14.273 line:92%
you build new friendships.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:16.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, sort of after
your acting career started

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:18.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were backpacking
around Europe,

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:22.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you had a co-star
who helped you and a friend ou

00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:25.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a way that I don't thin
many co-stars could.

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.253 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yeah, he really did.

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:29.455 size:84% position:42% line:92%
He really -- He took --

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were backpacking
through Europe. I was 19.

00:06:31.924 --> 00:06:33.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had just worked
with George on --

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
George Clooney --
on "The Descendants."

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:38.131
And he was like, "If you happe
to go to Europe this summer,

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:40.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
hit me up.
I've got a place in Italy.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:43.102
And I was like -- I remember
being in Italy with my frien

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:45.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
going, "Do you think, like -
Should I? Should I not?"

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:48.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he's kind of like my dad
in a weird way.

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:51.144
Like, he's just, like, you know,
given me so much life advice

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:53.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's been there for me
through so much.

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:54.414 line:92%
And she's like, "Yeah, why not?"

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:56.682
And so he was like, "Send me
your address. I'll send a car.

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "No, no, no,
we'll take a train.

00:06:58.418 --> 00:06:59.485 line:92%
It's so easy." And he was like

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Give me your
frickin' address, dude.

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:02.488 line:92%
Like, I'll send you a car.

00:07:02.488 --> 00:07:04.957 size:88% position:44%
And I remember we, like,
came out of our hostel.

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:06.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, we hadn't showered
in maybe five days.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:10.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
We stunk. We had our big
backpacks and mud on our shoes

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:13.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we get to
this fancy Lincoln Town Car.

00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:14.600 line:92%
And then we get to his house

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:16.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Chuckles ]
I remember that moment going

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
"He is the greatest human bein
of all time

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
for not, one, commenting
on our stench,

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:22.475 line:92%
and, two, for taking us in

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:23.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
and being like,
'I'm going to bathe you.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.946
I'm going to make sure you guys,
like, have a European experience

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:28.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's different
from the European experience

00:07:28.648 --> 00:07:30.316 size:78% position:39%
you've been having.'"
And it was just --

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:34.020
It was really magical in
all of the ways that it could be

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a 19-year-old seeing
the world for the first time

00:07:36.689 --> 00:07:40.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, did you have to,
after that, stay at a hostel

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the rest of your trip?
'Cause that would --

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:44.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would assume that would be
the hardest part.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know
what's actually incredible

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:48.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, he is
the most incredible man

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:51.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've ever met
in my life, period,

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:53.272 line:92%
apart from I guess Aaron.

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:55.007 line:92%
I guess I need to say that now

00:07:55.007 --> 00:07:57.577 line:92%
